Packet capture libraries (not included)
---------------------------------------

The sensor captures packets through the operating system's capture library,
which this project does not distribute:

- Linux and macOS: libpcap, provided by your operating system or package
  manager (BSD licence, https://www.tcpdump.org).
- Windows: Npcap, which you install yourself from https://npcap.com. Npcap is
  not open source and is licensed to you by Nmap Software LLC under its own
  terms, not by us. Its free licence covers installation on up to five
  systems; using it on more systems, or redistributing it, needs a commercial
  licence from its publisher. Read those terms before deploying the Windows
  sensor widely.


THIRD-PARTY TEST FIXTURES
-------------------------

Some tests run against real network device command output redistributed from
networktocode/ntc-templates (https://github.com/networktocode/ntc-templates),
licensed under the Apache License 2.0, Copyright 2015 Jason Edelman / Network
to Code, LLC. The output was sanitised (addresses rewritten to documentation
ranges, serial numbers and credential-shaped text redacted) and is kept, with
the project's licence file and a provenance record, under
shared/deviceinterrogation/testdata/real/. These files are used by tests only
and are not in the released binaries.


